You are an operator on a depot floor. Each round a crate is placed on the floor and you move it to one of {% if bay_identity.is_marked() %}the loading bays on that floor{% else %}the {{ bay_count }} loading bays{% endif %}.

The floor is a {{ grid_size }}x{{ grid_size }} grid of squares. Row 1 is the top row and column 1 is the left-hand one, and a square is written row then column, so 3,5 is row 3, column 5.{% if bay_identity.is_marked() %} Each bay is marked with a {{ bay_identity.value }}, and a bay is named by its {{ bay_identity.value }}.{% else %} A bay is named by the square it stands on.{% endif %}{% if has_pallets %} Pallets block some squares and a crate cannot be taken through them.{% endif %} Each round's briefing draws your floor: {{ bay_identity.crate_mark() }} where {% if crates_each > 1 %}your crates start{% else %}the crate starts{% endif %},{% if has_pallets %} # a pallet,{% endif %}{% if bay_identity.is_marked() %} each bay as its {{ bay_identity.value }}, . an open square. The briefing also lists the bays the depot has assigned you this round, each by its {{ bay_identity.value }} and its square. Your floor holds only those bays, and which {{ bay_identity.value }}s you are assigned and where they stand changes every round.{% else %} B a bay, . an open square. The briefing also gives the squares of the bays the depot has assigned you this round. Leaving {% if crates_each > 1 %}a crate{% else %}the crate{% endif %} on a bay you were not assigned scores nothing, and which bays you are assigned changes every round.{% endif %}{% if crates_each > 1 %} A bay takes one crate, so two of your crates on one bay score one delivery between them.{% endif %}

{% if crates_each > 1 %}You work {{ crates_each }} crates at once, each named by its marking on the readout, and every action says which crate it is for. The crates share one step budget. {% endif %}You move {% if crates_each > 1 %}a crate{% else %}the crate{% endif %} one square at a time with haul, choosing each time how to carry it: drag it along the floor, put it on a sled, or put it on a cart. All three cover one square. You can also stand by beside {% if crates_each > 1 %}a crate{% else %}the crate{% endif %}, or pack ice around it; neither moves it. Call finish when {% if crates_each > 1 %}a crate{% else %}the crate{% endif %} is where you want it to stay. If the round ends before you do, the square it stands on counts.{% if targets_per_round > 1 %}

Each round holds {{ targets_per_round }} targets, and each target assigns bays of its own the same way. Once every crate has been left for a target, you are given the next one: its bays, drawn on the same floor, and the crate where you left it. You move the crate on from there. Each target scores on its own.{% endif %}

